sp.p:
Right, lady; I am Sir Wilfull Witwoud, so I write myself;
no offense to anybody, I hope; and nephew to the Lady
Wishfort of this mansion.

Do, wrap thyself up like a wood louse, and dream revenge;
and hear me, if thou canst learn to write by tomorrow
morning, pen me a challenge. I’ll carry it for thee.

p.seg:
A woman’s hand? No, madam, that’s no woman’s hand;
I see that already. That’s somebody whose throat must be
cut.

sp.p:
How, how! I heard the villain was in the house indeed;
and now I remember, my niece went away abruptly, when
Sir Wilfull was to have made his addresses.
